<title>CHILE: Canada's Breakwater buys Chile zinc mine.</title>
<headline>Canada's Breakwater buys Chile zinc mine.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian mining company Breakwater Resources Ltd said it has bought Chilean zinc and gold mine El Toqui from Barrick Gold Corp for $6 million plus working capital.</p>
<p>El Toqui is expected to produce 70,000 tonnes of zinc concentrates with a grade of 48.8 percent and 3,000 tonnes of gold concentrates this year, said the spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The mine hopes to increase its zinc output by 20 percent next year, she said.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
